                        [ 'Shop or brand', 'Boards, cases and short-run gifts', 'Material, packing and handover' ],
                    ],
                ],
                [ 'p', 'On steel and anodised aluminium, the result depends on the material and laser source. Check contrast and scorching on wood, and tell customers if engraving a coated item may reveal the layer underneath. Glass and crystal require a separate choice of technology and a test.' ],
                [ 'h2', 'How do you collect names and prevent mistakes?' ],
                [ 'p', 'Keep the offer short: a few tested products, legible designs and a limited choice of typefaces. For each order record the item, option, exact wording, contact details needed to fulfil it and collection method. Do not collect more information than you need.' ],
                [
                    'ul',
                    [ 'Ask customers to write a name in block capitals or enter it themselves; check accents and capitalisation.', 'Show the wording for approval and agree who gives final sign-off. Request a logo file suitable for processing.', 'Assign order numbers and put them on the products and packaging. Keep the list linking numbers to customers separately.', 'Agree with the organiser how to collect the list, the deadline for changes, who handles corrections and how the data will be transferred securely.' ],
                ],
                [ 'p', 'When taking orders at an event, do not leave a list of personal details where other guests can see it. After fulfilment, follow your privacy procedures and the way your business actually operates.' ],
                [ 'h2', 'Workshop and laser choice' ],
                [ 'p', 'Choose a laser for the material and required finish, not just its portability. Before a batch, test the same surface and check the fixture, lettering size and settings. Save the settings and compare the result with the approved design.' ],
                [ 'p', 'The xTool F2 combines a 5 W infrared laser for marking metals and some plastics with a 15 W diode for selected materials such as wood and leather. Its 50 MP camera helps position a design; refresh the image manually after moving the item. A compatible rotary attachment can hold cylindrical objects.' ],
                [ 'p', 'The F2 is a Class 4 laser intended for professional use. xTool requires trained operators, a laser safety officer and safeguards and eye protection suited to its beams, including 445 ± 15, 655 ± 5 and 1064 ± 5 nm. The manufacturer prohibits using the F2 in residential areas, public places or around children or untrained people. Take orders at the stand and operate the machine in a properly controlled workshop according to its instructions.' ],
                [ 'products', '9163846877397' ],
                [ 'p', 'For some glass or crystal projects, xTool offers the F2 Ultra UV. Capabilities depend on the item and configuration, so check the material and test it before accepting the order. Do not assume one laser and one setting will suit every product.' ],
                [ 'products', '9187692970197' ],
                [ 'h2', 'How do you plan production and handover?' ],
                [ 'p', 'Work backwards from the agreed handover date: allow for file preparation, testing, workshop production, checks, packing and any delivery. Leave a margin for corrections and failed items. If you do not have every guest’s details yet, agree with the organiser when you will receive them.' ],
                [
                    'ul',
                    [ 'Before the event: prepare designs, check the material, make samples and agree prices and approval.', 'At the event: take complete orders, check spelling and confirm the agreed date and collection method.', 'After the event: group orders by material and settings, then engrave them in the workshop.', 'Before handover: compare the wording against the approved list, inspect the items and pack them under the correct order numbers.' ],
                ],
                [ 'p', 'If a customer wants to change the wording after approval, explain before production whether that is still possible. An engraving cannot always be removed without leaving a mark, so do not alter a finished product without agreement.' ],
                [ 'h2', 'How should you price personalised gifts?' ],
                [ 'p', 'You can quote per item or offer an organiser a package. Either way, include the item, design preparation, samples and rejects, workshop production time, stand staffing, packing, transport and delivery. If you charge a separate setup fee, do not include that fee a second time in the unit price.' ],
                [ 'p', 'Set out the quantity, available products, number of designs and revisions, deadline for details, approval process and handover method. For a package, agree what happens to orders above the limit. Say whether delivery is included and confirm the terms before work begins.' ],
                [ 'h2', 'Safety in the workshop and at the stand' ],
                [ 'p', 'In the workshop, select extraction and ventilation for the machine and material. A filter does not remove every gas, and the absence of smell does not prove the air is safe. Do not process unknown materials or PVC. Never leave a running laser unattended; follow the manufacturer’s fire and safety requirements.' ],
                [ 'p', 'A stand that only takes orders and distributes finished items needs no running laser. Agree its location, hours, display rules, fees and any power needed for order-taking equipment with the organiser. Clearly explain collection and store products and customer details securely.' ],
                [ 'h2', 'Frequently asked questions about engraving for events' ],
                [ 'h3', 'Can the xTool F2 be used around guests?' ],
                [ 'p', 'No. xTool classifies the F2 as a Class 4 laser and prohibits its use in residential areas, public places or around untrained people and children. Take the order at the stand and engrave it later in a properly controlled workshop.' ],
                [ 'h3', 'Can a guest collect an item during the event?' ],
                [ 'p', 'Yes, if the order was taken and completed in the workshop before the event and the organiser has agreed to hand out finished items at the stand. Orders taken during the event need a separately agreed later collection or delivery.' ],
                [ 'h3', 'What if I do not know the names before the event?' ],
                [ 'p', 'Let guests choose an item and place an order during the event. Check the spelling before approval and explain when and how you will deliver the finished item after workshop production.' ],
                [ 'h3', 'How many orders can I accept?' ],
                [ 'p', 'Time a test design, add preparation, checking and packing, then consider your available workshop capacity. Agree a limit with the organiser before taking orders; actual throughput depends on the item and design.' ],
                [ 'h3', 'Is a portable laser suitable for a public stand?' ],
                [ 'p', 'Portability or an air purifier alone does not establish safe working conditions. For the F2, xTool rules out use in residential areas, public places or around untrained people. Check the particular machine’s instructions and workspace requirements before planning production.' ],
                [ 'h2', 'Discuss your choice of machine' ],
                [ 'p', 'Book a free online demo and ask which machine suits the products you plan to make in your workshop. Before accepting an order, check the configuration and test the customer’s material or a suitable sample.' ],
            ],
